{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A dashed barline.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/Style\/dashed","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/Style"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor\/style\/dashed"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dashed"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"metadata":{"title":"MXLBarline.StyleColor.Style.dashed","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV10StyleColorV0D0O6dashedyA2GmF","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dashed"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"title":"MXLBarline","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/StyleColor/Style/dashed":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/Style\/dashed","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dashed"}],"title":"MXLBarline.StyleColor.Style.dashed","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor\/style\/dashed","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dashed barline."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/StyleColor":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor","title":"MXLBarline.StyleColor","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StyleColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StyleColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bar-style-color type contains barline style and color information."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/StyleColor/Style":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/stylecolor\/style","title":"MXLBarline.StyleColor.Style","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Style"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The bar-style type represents barline style information. Choices are regular, dotted, dashed, heavy, light-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"light, light-heavy, heavy-light, heavy-heavy, tick (a short stroke through the top line), short (a partial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"barline between the 2nd and 4th lines), and none."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor\/Style"}}}